Z||000003||Brandon86SE||12-13-2001||03:23 PM||||That's good, been a while since I've heard it.  Since we got a Canada vs. US thing going on here, I'll add one of my own.<P>A teacher in an American kindergarten class asks the class: "Who here is an American?", and she raises her hand.  All the kids want to be like their teacher, and raise their hands as well.  All but one.  The teacher notices this, and questions the little girl on it.  "Why didn't you raise your hand?"  The little girl replies "Because I'm a Canadian."  The teacher is getting annoyed, and asks "Well, why are you a Canadian?"  The little girl says "My mother is Canadian, and my father is Canadian, so I am too."  The teacher starts to get infuriated at this, and yells back "Well, if your mother was a moron, and your father was a moron, then what would you be?"  The little girl, pauses, and thinks, then replies: "Well, I suppose then I'd be an American."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I love that one!<P>Brandon||||reg||10
